\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Father, who on man dost shower 
\par Gifts of plenty from Thy dower,
\par To Thy people give the power
\par All Thy gifts to use aright.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Give pure happiness in leisure,
\par Temperance in every pleasure,
\par Holy use of earthly treasure,
\par Bodies clear and spirits bright.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Lift from this and every nation
\par All that brings us degradation;
\par Quell the forces of temptation;
\par Put Thy enemies to flight.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Be with us, Thy strength supplying,
\par That with energy undying,
\par Every foe of man defying,
\par We may rally to the fight.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thou who art our Captain ever,
\par Lead us unto great endeavour;
\par May Thy Church the world deliver:
\par Give us wisdom, courage, might.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Father, who hast sought and found us,
\par Son of God, whose love has bound us,
\par Holy Ghost, within us, round us-
\par Hear us, Godhead infinite.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

